<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · lake</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lake Pichola</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lake Pichola is an artificial lake at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udaipur">Udaipur</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajasthan">Rajasthan</a>, created according to tradition in 1362 when a Banjara grain trader dammed a stream. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/udai-singh-ii">Udai Singh II</a> enlarged it after founding Udaipur on its eastern shore in 1559, and its islands and banks hold the City Palace, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jag-mandir">Jag Mandir</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-palace">Lake Palace</a>, making it the centre of the city's royal architecture.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lake-pichola.jpg" alt="Lake Pichola" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uri Sittan Tripo · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Udaipur_Lake_India.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
